# Production env template for the Docker Compose stack.
# Copy to /opt/hedgefun/.env on the VPS, fill real values, chmod 600. NOT committed.

# --- Postgres (compose `db` service) ---
POSTGRES_USER=hedgefun
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME_STRONG
POSTGRES_DB=hedgefun

# --- App runtime ---
# host=db resolves on the internal compose network; password must match POSTGRES_PASSWORD.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://hedgefun:CHANGE_ME_STRONG@db:5432/hedgefun?schema=public
PRIVY_APP_SECRET=CHANGE_ME_ROTATED_SECRET
# Secret for hashing referral-click IP/UA (cross-browser attribution fallback). Generate with
# `openssl rand -hex 32`. If UNSET, the IP/UA fallback is disabled gracefully (cookie path still
# works); set it in prod to catch the in-app-browser → system-browser case. See src/lib/refclick.ts.
# required in production since 2026-09-02 — the app refuses to boot without it
REFERRAL_HASH_SECRET=CHANGE_ME_RANDOM_HEX_32
# Needed at BUILD (inlined into client bundle) AND runtime — compose passes it as a build arg.
NEXT_PUBLIC_PRIVY_APP_ID=CHANGE_ME_PRIVY_APP_ID
NODE_ENV=production

# NEXT_PUBLIC_SHARE_BASE_URL — optional, defaults to https://app.hedgeyour.fun (src/lib/share.ts).
#   Override only for the Android build to aim invite links at a Play Store URL (deferred deep link).
# POLYMARKET_API_BASE — optional, code defaults to https://gamma-api.polymarket.com
# DEV_USER_EMAIL — intentionally UNSET in production (gates dev bypasses in src/lib/dev.ts)

# --- Hedge engine (phase 2, workstream A — S1 wallet hedge) ---
# Read-only wallet exposure = balances (Helius) × prices (Jupiter). Jupiter's price API needs NO key
# at our volumes (src/lib/prices.ts). If HELIUS_API_KEY is unset, /api/hedge/wallet returns 502
# (exposure_unavailable) — there are no balances to hedge against; it never guesses.
HELIUS_API_KEY=CHANGE_ME_HELIUS_API_KEY
# Birdeye Wallet PnL powers ONLY the optional "you bought at ~$X" narrative line (avg buy cost, D4).
# Beta wallet APIs are hard-capped 5 rps / 75 rpm, so it is cached in WalletSnapshot with a TTL and
# NEVER called synchronously per request. If unset (or the cap/endpoint fails), the card still renders
# WITHOUT the narrative line (graceful degradation) — it is never required for a suggestion.
BIRDEYE_API_KEY=CHANGE_ME_BIRDEYE_API_KEY
# JUPITER_PRICE_BASE / BIRDEYE_API_BASE / BIRDEYE_PNL_PATH — optional overrides (HELIUS_API_BASE is gone: balances
# moved to JSON-RPC on HELIUS_RPC_BASE after Helius retired the v0 balances endpoint, 2026-09-15);
#   code defaults to https://api.helius.xyz , https://lite-api.jup.ag/price/v3 ,
#   https://public-api.birdeye.so , and /wallet/v2/pnl respectively.
# NLU edge only (D2, spec §5) — OPTIONAL. Powers a SINGLE constrained small-model call in the S2
# free-text path (/api/hedge/search), invoked ONLY when deterministic alias/FTS matching falls below
# the confidence threshold. The LLM extracts { category, entities, keywords } and the deterministic
# search RE-RUNS with them — it NEVER picks a side/size/market (D1). If UNSET (or the call fails /
# times out), the search degrades straight to the discovery fallback. Safe to leave unset in dev.
# Provider-agnostic: any OpenAI-compatible /chat/completions endpoint (OpenRouter, DeepSeek, Kimi,
# MiniMax, GLM, OpenAI). Only the key is required — base and model have defaults.
NLU_API_KEY=CHANGE_ME_NLU_API_KEY
# NLU_API_BASE — optional; defaults to https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# NLU_MODEL    — optional; defaults to deepseek/deepseek-v4
# HEDGE_NLU_LOG_RAW — optional debug flag. UNSET/anything-but-1 (default): the NLU edge logs a
#   sha256 fingerprint of the free text + the parsed output + latency (replayable, no PII). Set to
#   "1" ONLY for local debugging to log the RAW user query verbatim — never enable in production
#   (free-text hedge queries can carry personal plans). See src/lib/hedge/nlu.ts.

# --- Monitoring / alerting (all optional — features no-op when unset) ---
# GlitchTip DSN (Sentry protocol) + ops Telegram — error capture + alerting (src/lib/glitchtip.ts).
SENTRY_DSN=
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=
# Passphrase encrypting every dump before it leaves this host (openssl aes-256-cbc, pbkdf2).
# Generate with `openssl rand -base64 48`; keep a copy in the password manager and NOT on VPS2
# — unset means the offsite copies of user emails/balances travel in plaintext (nightly WARN).
BACKUP_ENC_PASSPHRASE=
# Health-check URLs pinged by poller / backup / watchdog as uptime heartbeats (UptimeRobot etc).
POLLER_HC_URL=
BACKUP_HC_URL=
WATCHDOG_HC_URL=
# Set to 1 to run the watchdog in observe-only mode (logs, never auto-restarts). The burn-in
# default was 1; with real money live it must be 0 — plain Docker never restarts a container on a
# failing healthcheck, so a wedged (not crashed) poller stops settlement and deposit detection
# until a human reads Telegram.
WATCHDOG_OBSERVE=0

# Polygon RPC used for deposit detection, chain-side settlement proof and redemption reads.
# Unset it falls back to the free public polygon-bor-rpc.publicnode.com — fine for dev, a single
# unkeyed point of failure for real money. Set a keyed endpoint (Alchemy/QuickNode/dRPC) in prod.
POLYGON_RPC_URL=
# Comma-separated keyed fallbacks, tried in order after POLYGON_RPC_URL when it fails at the
# transport level (Alchemy in prod). publicnode is always the last resort, unlisted. An endpoint
# that refuses an eth_getLogs range (Alchemy Free: 10 blocks) keeps serving eth_call and is skipped
# for logs only. See src/lib/polygon.ts.
POLYGON_RPC_FALLBACK_URLS=


# REAL_MONEY_EMAILS / REAL_MONEY_TWITTER are GONE. They were the alpha allowlist that kept the
# real-money path to a couple of hand-picked accounts while it was being written; access is now
# open to anyone who explicitly consents (src/lib/real.ts). Leaving them set does nothing —
# delete them from a prod .env so nobody reads them as an active control.
# Public Polymarket builder code (attribution in signed orders + bridge deposits). NOT a secret,
# but unset = attribution silently vanishes.
POLYMARKET_BUILDER_CODE=
# Same value, exposed to the browser: the builder CODE is a public attribution tag (never the key/secret).
# PROD: putting this in the VPS .env does NOTHING. NEXT_PUBLIC_* is inlined at BUILD time, so it has
# to reach the image as a docker build-arg — it is a GitHub Actions secret of the same name, wired
# through deploy.yml into the Dockerfile. Set it here only for local `npm run dev`.
NEXT_PUBLIC_POLYMARKET_BUILDER_CODE=
# Builder API credentials (SERVER ONLY — authenticate relayer ops; never reach a client bundle).
POLYMARKET_BUILDER_API_KEY=
POLYMARKET_BUILDER_SECRET=
POLYMARKET_BUILDER_PASSPHRASE=
# AES-256-GCM key (64 hex chars) for encrypted-at-rest user CLOB creds. Keep OUT of DB backups.
REAL_CREDS_KEY=
# Exact app origin for money-route same-origin checks (S8). Unset = check disabled (dev).
APP_ORIGIN=
# Where the signed order is POSTED. Unset/anything else = this server posts it. `browser` = the
# server validates, claims and stops, and the BROWSER posts with its own SecureClient, reporting
# only the order id to /api/real/posted (which reads the order back from the exchange before
# booking a cent — a client-supplied receipt is never accepted either way).
# Set this to `browser` whenever the host is geoblocked: Polymarket answers our VPS with "Trading
# restricted in your region", and that check is about the TRADER, so a server post puts the wrong
# party in front of it. REAL_RECONCILE_URL/SECRET below must be set with it — the orphan sweep is
# what recovers an order whose browser died before reporting.
REAL_ORDER_LOCUS=
# Order reconciliation (plan §2.1 step 6). The poller is SDK-free, so it PINGS the app:
# REAL_RECONCILE_URL is the app's own /api/real/reconcile, REAL_RECONCILE_SECRET is the shared
# secret both sides use (unset on either side = reconciliation simply does not run; the route
# 503s rather than reconcile unauthenticated).
REAL_RECONCILE_URL=
REAL_RECONCILE_SECRET=

# ---- Tokenized stocks (xStocks on Solana — Stocklana) ----
# All optional overrides; the defaults are the public endpoints. HELIUS_API_KEY (above) now also
# powers real-buy confirmation (getTransaction) — without it /api/stocks/real/confirm answers 502;
# the paper stock deck does not need it.
XSTOCKS_API_BASE=
JUPITER_SWAP_BASE=
HELIUS_RPC_BASE=

# Fee sponsorship for REAL stock buys/sells: OUR fee-payer key, base58 64-byte ed25519 secret
# (Phantom "export private key"). A first-time buyer holds USDC and no SOL, so without this they
# cannot transact at all. Fund the address with SOL: it pays the tx fee + priority (capped by
# STOCK_SPONSOR_MAX_PRIORITY_LAMPORTS) and FRONTS ~0.0016 SOL of rent per new xStock token account,
# which comes back when the user sells the position in full (the sale closes the account, rent to
# the sponsor). Unset or malformed => sponsorship is simply off: buys fall back to the self-paid
# path (the wallet pays its own fee) and real SELLS are unavailable. NEVER commit a real value.
STOCK_SPONSOR_SECRET=
